A reverse-mode autograd engine in C, just big
enough to train karpathy's microGPT.


Ops record onto a tape that backward walks in
reverse. The tape and a 256 KiB arena for all
activations and gradients are allocated statically,
TigerBeetle style, so nothing is allocated after
startup and a training step resets in O(1).


Attention is composed from 12 primitive float64 ops
like matmul, softmax, rmsnorm and causal mask, each
with its backward right next to its forward.


    $ make parity
    trained 1000 steps in 0.101s
    passed parity check (max |diff| 5.7e-15)
    inference (random sampled name): kaonle


Training from karpathy's initial weights reproduces
his final weights to within 1e-11. Every op and the
full model are also checked against finite
differences under ASan and UBSan.


References:

- autograd.lean: https://github.com/sueszli/autograd.lean
- microGPT: https://karpathy.github.io/2026/02/12/microgpt/
- TigerStyle: https://github.com/tigerbeetle/tigerbeetle/blob/main/docs/TIGER_STYLE.md
- Hacker News: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46285424
